WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.223
Tesla added more than 260 cybercabs in Austin last month, while NHTSA reviews school zone speeds. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 639. The Texas Robotaxi fleet is now past 300 vehicles. The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, or NHTSA, is also reviewing federal compliance for vehicles that have no steering wheels or pedals. That regulatory timeline now directly limits paid unsupervised service and margin expansion. South Korea's

00:00:30.223 --> 00:00:35.883
September auto exports dropped 5.5%, according to data compiled by big-go finance.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:39.443
The total came in at approximately $6.1 billion.

00:00:40.363 --> 00:00:43.183
Tesla's Model Y led domestic sales in the month.

00:00:43.863 --> 00:00:48.583
Registration and sales data show the Model Y outsold other models in its category during

00:00:48.583 --> 00:00:49.143
the period.

00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:53.103
The figures come from official export statistics released for the month.

00:00:53.643 --> 00:00:58.383
The Model Y gained ground inside the country even as the broader Korean automotive sector

00:00:58.383 --> 00:00:59.223
faces pressure.

00:00:59.223 --> 00:01:03.280
A Porsche 911 owner ordered a Model Y performance.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.600
The owner had driven the 911 as a daily car before placing that order.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:14.760
The driver cited full self-driving supervised or FSD supervised ride quality and GROC integration

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.040
as the reasons for switching.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.240
Tesla shared the story on its official account after the order was placed.

00:01:21.207 --> 00:01:25.207
Tesla Roddy released its full review of the updated Model Y L variant.

00:01:25.207 --> 00:01:30.207
The video covers driving impressions and feature changes on the longer wheelbase version.

00:01:30.647 --> 00:01:35.607
The review examines how the extended wheelbase alters interior space compared with the standard

00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:39.667
model Y. It also looks at how that extra length changes handling.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:45.690
The new Roadster was called beautifully pointless in a top gear review after its recent unveiling.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.710
Yahoo autos carried the piece, which acknowledges the vehicle's extreme performance targets,

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.890
yet questions its everyday utility.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.730
The magazine compares the car to a Veyron.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:00.610
It notes the limited practicality of a two-seat supercar with one-time-use thrusters.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:06.230
The review contrasts the engineering spectacle with real-world driving scenarios where those

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.630
specialized features would see infrequent use.

00:02:09.641 --> 00:02:13.981
Franz von Holeshausen said that same Roadster will receive limited FSD.

00:02:14.481 --> 00:02:19.361
The chief designer noted the extreme windshield angle and driver-centric setup in a reddit

00:02:19.361 --> 00:02:20.141
discussion thread.

00:02:20.141 --> 00:02:23.861
Those elements limit full supervised FSD deployment.

00:02:24.401 --> 00:02:29.201
Von Holtzhausen explained that the car's design prioritizes track and performance driving

00:02:29.201 --> 00:02:33.021
over the sensor layout required for comprehensive supervised autonomy.

00:02:33.561 --> 00:02:38.981
The limited FSD capability is a deliberate engineering choice rather than a temporary restriction.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:45.190
Tiktok flags certain Roadster unveiling videos as artificial intelligence generated content.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:49.930
Tesla Roddy noted that multiple user-uploaded videos appeared with the platforms

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:55.130
AI-generated label. Tesla conducted the unveiling with physical vehicles and live

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:59.210
demonstrations in Texas. Viewers encountered the warning on footage that

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:03.510
included the car's butterfly doors and nitrogen thruster sequences. The

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.070
account highlighted the discrepancy between the physical event and the automated

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:11.661
labeling. Drive Tesla Canada released a winter driving guide for Tesla

00:03:11.661 --> 00:03:15.621
vehicles. The article addresses cold weather operation across Canadian

00:03:15.621 --> 00:03:21.581
provinces. It covers range loss, charging behavior, and winter tire recommendations. Lower

00:03:21.581 --> 00:03:26.001
temperatures reduce battery efficiency and preconditioning and tire choice affect daily

00:03:26.001 --> 00:03:31.501
range. Owners are advised on optimal charging speeds in sub-zero conditions and on selecting

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:34.721
tires that maintain traction without compromising efficiency.

00:03:35.401 --> 00:03:40.241
The guide compiles practical steps drawn from owner experiences and Tesla's own recommendations

00:03:40.241 --> 00:03:45.531
for regions with prolonged freezing temperatures. A homeowner seeking additional storage

00:03:45.531 --> 00:03:50.151
capacity learned that third-party batteries would void the existing warranty on an installed

00:03:50.151 --> 00:03:50.811
power wall.

00:03:51.351 --> 00:03:55.911
A newsbreak report said only official Tesla units would keep the original terms intact.

00:03:56.491 --> 00:03:59.231
The owner had planned to expand an existing installation.

00:03:59.791 --> 00:04:02.951
The restriction applies even when the hardware is technically compatible.

00:04:03.511 --> 00:04:08.391
It applies specifically to maintaining coverage for the original power wall and associated components.

00:04:09.507 --> 00:04:13.887
Ample opened Australia's largest electric vehicle or EV charging hub.

00:04:13.887 --> 00:04:18.567
The Driven reports the facility currently leads Australian fast-charging capacity.

00:04:18.907 --> 00:04:23.467
It opened with multiple high-power stalls and amenities aimed at long-distance travelers.

00:04:24.207 --> 00:04:28.347
Tesla's forthcoming supercharger site is described as having 37 bays.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:33.047
That location is expected to surpass the new ample record once it is operational.

00:04:34.157 --> 00:04:37.817
SpaceX president Gwynne Schottwell quietly followed Tesla on X.

00:04:38.357 --> 00:04:43.137
Tesla Roddy reported that the follow came days before SpaceX reports third-quarter results.

00:04:43.137 --> 00:04:47.797
The move drew attention amid ongoing merger speculation between the two companies.

00:04:48.417 --> 00:04:52.677
Observers noted the timing as SpaceX prepares to release earnings that could influence

00:04:52.677 --> 00:04:54.657
any potential transaction structure.

00:04:55.217 --> 00:04:57.997
Whole Mars catalog first highlighted the account change.

00:04:58.437 --> 00:05:03.157
The follow occurred while merger discussions remain active in analyst commentary and investor

00:05:03.157 --> 00:05:03.577
forums.

00:05:04.589 --> 00:05:09.529
Seeking Alpha argues that Tesla's focus on high profile projects risks diverting attention

00:05:09.529 --> 00:05:11.429
from core profitability challenges.

00:05:11.429 --> 00:05:16.489
images. The analysis points to ongoing margin pressure. It questions whether the emphasis

00:05:16.489 --> 00:05:21.469
on future programs helps near-term results. The piece examines how investor narratives

00:05:21.469 --> 00:05:26.829
around upcoming products may overshadow current delivery and margin trends. It suggests the

00:05:26.829 --> 00:05:31.469
company's valuation could face continued pressure until vehicle and energy margins stabilize.

00:05:32.129 --> 00:05:36.289
The commentary frames the distraction risk as a factor that could extend valuation

00:05:36.289 --> 00:05:39.769
compression, if core operations do not show clearer improvement.

00:05:40.708 --> 00:05:47.328
A vehicle without a steering wheel or pedals must still meet the same federal motor vehicle safety standards written for cars that have both.

00:05:47.908 --> 00:05:54.088
The cybercabs design therefore triggers extra scrutiny precisely because those standards assume human controls exist.

00:05:54.668 --> 00:06:02.508
The absence of those controls turns every incident into a test of whether the vehicle itself, rather than a driver, can be held to the original rule set.

00:06:02.508 --> 00:06:06.508
But the Austin fleet grew from fewer than 40 vehicles in roughly a month.

00:06:07.128 --> 00:06:13.208
319 cybercabs and 420 model Y Robotaxies were registered in Texas by October 10.

00:06:13.648 --> 00:06:18.588
That scale arrives while the agency is still determining how a car lacking traditional interfaces

00:06:18.588 --> 00:06:21.028
complies with standards written decades earlier.

00:06:21.568 --> 00:06:26.288
Each additional vehicle multiplies the number of edge cases regulators must evaluate before

00:06:26.288 --> 00:06:28.508
any unsupervised approval can be granted.

00:06:28.508 --> 00:06:33.708
For Tesla, the regulatory timeline now sits alongside production and software milestones

00:06:33.708 --> 00:06:35.568
as a direct constraint on revenue.

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:40.528
Until the agency completes its reviews, the company cannot expand the paid service beyond

00:06:40.528 --> 00:06:41.008
Austin.

00:06:41.588 --> 00:06:46.228
The same standards that once protected drivers now require new validation methods for systems

00:06:46.228 --> 00:06:47.628
that replace them entirely.

00:06:48.588 --> 00:06:53.388
NHTSA's preliminary evaluation and its separate federal compliance review both hinge on

00:06:53.388 --> 00:06:55.308
data that only the vehicle can generate.

00:06:55.308 --> 00:07:00.028
Tesla's ability to supply that data at scale will determine whether the current Austin

00:07:00.028 --> 00:07:02.468
operation can serve as a template for other cities.

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:07.148
The economics of a robotaxi fleet shift once regulatory clearance arrives.

00:07:07.748 --> 00:07:12.288
Each day of continued review delays the moment when those vehicles can operate without safety

00:07:12.288 --> 00:07:13.788
drivers or remote monitors.

00:07:14.408 --> 00:07:18.968
The capital already committed to the fleet sits idle in terms of full margin revenue until

00:07:18.968 --> 00:07:20.068
the rules are clarified.

00:07:20.708 --> 00:07:25.068
In that sense, the regulatory process functions as a hidden production bottleneck that

00:07:25.068 --> 00:07:30.768
no factory expansion can bypass. Tesla's next earnings call may therefore be judged as much

00:07:30.768 --> 00:07:36.832
on regulatory progress as on vehicle delivery numbers. Before we go, SpaceX's third quarter

00:07:36.832 --> 00:07:41.452
results are the next scheduled release on the calendar. That's your Tesla news for today.

